              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Hamilton's defence was that the state debts were incurred for a common cause, so relieving them was rough justice. If so, states the 1793 audit found had over-paid should have received more relief. They did: $6.12 vs $2.67 per head (exact permutation p = 0.047; Spearman rho = 0.55).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "Segoe UI",
                      "fontSize": "10pt",
